{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfkC93d4CtHSAfJ6VbQoE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HzPDYxGuGYuNH4s52iQVaq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/releases/_next/cli-confidence-grade-and-clean-stdout.md","content":"# vNEXT — CLI shows the stated confidence grade and keeps stdout clean\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-06\n**PR:** #N\n**Type:** minor\n\n## Summary\n\nThe confidence block printed by `run.py` now shows the grade the data layer stated, its weakest input and each component's own grade, instead of a printed Python dictionary. When a response states no grade the block shows the ratings and says so. Console log records now go to standard error, so standard output holds only the outcome.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `run.py`: the confidence block shows `grade`, `weakest input` and `component <name>` lines read from the response; a missing grade renders \"grade: not stated by the data layer\".\n- `logging_config.yaml`: the console handler writes to standard error. Levels, the log file and `LOG_LEVEL` are unchanged.\n- `--json` standard output is exactly one JSON document.\n- Out of scope: rendering a Modelled grade's backtest block.\n\n## Local deployment\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Manual steps\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\ngit checkout main && git pull\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_run_cli.py tests/unit/test_logging_config.py -q\n```\n\nExpected: the tests pass with no failures or errors.\n\n## Rollback\n\n`git checkout` the previous tag. Nothing else needs reversing.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":391,"cache_read_input_tokens":45284,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":391},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d720d32-2e38-4c91-ace7-0965c0cbf441","uuid":"5abcf151-c63b-4b70-8224-6062d6e768de","timestamp":"2026-10-06T02:27:14.210Z","request_id":"req_011CfkC93PeoNkMwEK3GBVWu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HzPDYxGuGYuNH4s52iQVaq":{"file_path":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/releases/_next/cli-confidence-grade-and-clean-stdout.md","content":"# vNEXT — CLI shows the stated confidence grade and keeps stdout clean\n\n**Date:** 2026-10-06\n**PR:** #N\n**Type:** minor\n\n## Summary\n\nThe confidence block printed by `run.py` now shows the grade the data layer stated, its weakest input and each component's own grade, instead of a printed Python dictionary. When a response states no grade the block shows the ratings and says so. Console log records now go to standard error, so standard output holds only the outcome.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `run.py`: the confidence block shows `grade`, `weakest input` and `component <name>` lines read from the response; a missing grade renders \"grade: not stated by the data layer\".\n- `logging_config.yaml`: the console handler writes to standard error. Levels, the log file and `LOG_LEVEL` are unchanged.\n- `--json` standard output is exactly one JSON document.\n- Out of scope: rendering a Modelled grade's backtest block.\n\n## Local deployment\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Manual steps\n\nNothing to do.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\ngit checkout main && git pull\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_run_cli.py tests/unit/test_logging_config.py -q\n```\n\nExpected: the tests pass with no failures or errors.\n\n## Rollback\n\n`git checkout` the previous tag. Nothing else needs reversing.\n"}}}
